s-visible`, `data-disabled`"],[1386,"**Shared structural containers.** These generic, layout-only components are the building blocks for composing a component's interior (a `Modal`, a card, a panel). They are semantic containers built on `Flex`, so they accept the same layout props (`direction`, `gap`, `alignItems`, `justifyContent`, `padding`, ...)."],[377,"**Shift + Tab**: Moves focus to the previous checkbox"],[276,"**Simplify tooltips**: If tooltips are complex, consider using simpler content or disabling them"],[214,"**Single and multi-series support**: Display one or multiple data series with grouped bars"],[1322,"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` to allow multiple values"],[912,"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"single\"` or `\"multiple\"`."],[1538,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, input, description, error, and composed controls; without it, the field follows the surrounding scope. An explicit `size` on a part still wins for that part"],[1008,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, input, steppers, description, and error; without it, the field follows the surrounding scope"],[1325,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets the label, trigger, and options, which open at the same size even though they render in a portal. Without it, the Select follows the surrounding scope"],[1177,"**Space**: Select the focused radio button"],[376,"**Space**: Toggles the focused checkbox"],[946,"**Space/Enter**: activate an item; **Escape**: close"],[1298,"**Space/Enter**: Select the focused segment"],[741,"**Sprite Sheet Creation**: A hidden SVG sprite sheet is automatically injected into the DOM containing symbol definitions"],[751,"**SSR Limitation**: Sprite references render empty until client-side hydration"],[1394,"**Standalone** - with no parent context it renders with its own structural defaults and looks the same everywhere."],[1007,"**Steppers**: A stepper is a `Group` holding `Button slot=\"decrement\"`, an `Input`, and `Button slot=\"increment\"`. Left empty, each button takes its icon and `variant=\"control\"` from the field, so no icon imports are needed. Compose a bare `Input` instead for a plain numeric input"],[250,"**Sticky axes**: Positioned absolutely to remain visible during scroll"],[239,"**Sticky y-axis**: The y-axis remains visible during horizontal scroll"],[691,"**Styling**: `className`, `style`, `data-*` attributes"],[735,"**SVG Parsing**: The fetched SVG string is parsed into a React element using `@bento/svg-parser`"],[375,"**Tab**: Moves focus to the next/previous checkbox"],[1174,"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the radio group"],[1296,"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the segmented controller"],[1566,"**The body is `<Text slot=\"body\">`**, once or as many times as the copy needs."],[1564,"**The eyebrow is `slot=\"eyebrow\"`**, on either a `Text` or a `Tag`. The two forms swap\nfreely, and a `Tag` is sized to pair with the lockup."],[1565,"**The title is `<Heading slot=\"title\">`.** Pick the level from the document outline, not the\nvisual size: `size` handles the visuals, so `level={1}` in an `xs` lockup is perfectly valid."],[1143,"**Titles overflow:** that's expected — titles truncate. Shorten the title."],[1624,"**ToggleButton Item:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"],[1623,"**ToggleButtonGroup Container:** `data-size`"],[254,"**Tooltips** use absolute positioning and scroll-aware calculations for accurate placement"],[243,"**Tooltips**: Show on both hover and focus for keyboard users"],[750,"**Trade-offs:**"],[692,"**Transform**: `rotate`, `flip` for icon transformations"],[1320,"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `ListBox` props (including `items` with a render function for a dynamic collection) plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `ListBox` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[949,"**Type to select**: jump to a matching item (string labels are used as `textValue`)"],[852,"**Typed Refs:** Refs are correctly typed based on the `as` value - `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>` works with `as=\"button\"`."],[223,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[686,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[892,"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."],[753,"**Use default mode** for SSR applications or when icons appear infrequently"],[754,"**Use sprite mode** when the same icons appear many times (navigation, lists, tables)"],[764,"**Use sprite mode**: For repeated icons, consider sprite mode which consolidates multiple icons into a single SVG sprite sheet, reducing DOM size and improving performance when the same icon appears multiple times"],[1011,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1324,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1537,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1009,"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"],[272,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[215,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[248,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[224,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[740,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[154,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[848,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[624,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1180,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1301,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[466,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[378,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1181,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1302,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[380,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1183,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1633,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1303,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[465,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[379,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1182,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[463,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[462,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[464,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[840,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[857,"`BoxContext` supplies default props to Boxes in its subtree. A `slots` map supplies defaults to\nnamed parts; each Box selects one with `slot`. Explicit consu